    "objectives": "# Scenario 4 — Add a medication with potential interactions\n\n## Context\nThe patient's doctor wants to add Ibuprofen for occasional joint pain management. However, Ibuprofen may interact with Warfarin and is generally contraindicated in chronic kidney disease.\n\n## Objectives\n1. Propose adding Ibuprofen as a medication activity, 400mg, every day at 13:00 after lunch.\n2. If the assistant flags a safety concern or drug interaction, acknowledge the warning and ask for a safer alternative.\n3. Accept whatever alternative the assistant suggests and confirm the change.\n4. Verify that the final medication decision is confirmed.\n\n## Notes\n- Do not insist on adding Ibuprofen if the assistant raises a contraindication — the goal is to test whether the system correctly identifies the risk.\n- The scenario is considered successful if either: (a) Ibuprofen is correctly flagged and an alternative is agreed upon, or (b) Ibuprofen is added with appropriate warnings documented."
